WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.420
<b>Spring is here.</b>

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:07.530
Happy New Year!

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.380
To all the people who helped us last year

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.950
and all the viewers who watched this show.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.990
Yeah, if you wanted to sneak in a New Year greeting

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.390
at the beginning of an episode,

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.290
you should have done it last week

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.420
since the last episode was about New Year's envelopes.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.840
Hey!

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.430
I can understand if you're too lazy to respond,

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.980
but that doesn't make it okay to fart!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.430
That's plain rude!

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.020
Hey!

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:30.910
<b>Kotatsu</b>

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.980
Do you think it's possible that humans evolved from kotatsu?

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:35.910
What are you talking about?

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.290
Humans are drawn to kotatsu by DNA.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.740
Isn't there a mythical creature that looks like this?

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.300
Maybe humans and kotatsu used to be one and the same.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.960
I've never seen anything like that before.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.620
And then evolution gave us what is now

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:53.420
humankind.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.610
That's a pretty biased example to use for humankind.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.810
So we're trying to reunite with the kotatsu!

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.690
You've finally realized the truth!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.690
It's time to unite with me, Gin-san!

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:08.620
I have a feeling this was devolution.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.280
<b>The End</b>

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:15.280
<b>Shinsengumi Station</b>

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.280
<b>New Year Greetings</b>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.150
Gantan.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.790
Gantan?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.150
Gantan.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.320
Ganpan.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.860
Antan.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:33.970
Anpan!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:41.830
Anpan!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.910
<b>The End</b>

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.670
<b>Recycling Center
Earth Defense Base</b>

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:49.670
Hey.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.460
Excuse me, can you buy this off me?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.720
Cut it out already.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.210
This isn't a dump.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.750
I'm not sure what's wrong, but the thermostat isn't working.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.650
You have to be stronger!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.560
I can't switch it off the strong setting.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.020
I thought the last segment ended!

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.950
Can I trade this for something kotatsu-like?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.290
We don't deal in human trade.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:16.410
Huh?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.730
Hey, you've got a nice one here.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.940
Wait, that's...

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:27.920
<b>When Sleeping Under a Kotatsu, Make Sure You Don't Burn Your Balls</b>

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.920
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose</b>

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.540
Good morning!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.520
Huh?

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.260
Again?

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.270
They're so hopeless.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.730
Hey!

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.330
You're going to catch a cold if you sleep under the kotatsu!

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.320
Cut that out! It's a disgrace!

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.660
You too, Sadaharu!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.400
It's the first episode of the new year, and you're just sitting around.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.980
Everything is within reach of the kotatsu.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.080
How lazy can you be?

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.110
Shut up.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.310
I'm staying here because it's cold.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.210
What's wrong with being lazy on New Year's, stupid?

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.800
You're lazy every single day of the year!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.310
Pachi-boy, I decided to

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.320
marry the kotatsu.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.450
I can't live without it.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:32.440
Everyone, Happy New Year!

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:32.400
The kotatsu doesn't want a bride who never moves.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:43.710
Thank you for coming to my concert on such a busy day to show your supportapoop!

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.690
Could you get out of there?

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:44.550
The fridge is empty because we haven't gone shopping recently.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.570
We don't have food for lunch.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.720
What? We don't need to go shopping.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.110
I've got lunch right here.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.970
Piping hot meat buns.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.200
Uh, that's disgusting!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.880
You're not supposed to use a kotatsu that way!

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.950
Fine, you don't get any then.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.690
Gin-chan, where's the mustard?

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.180
We have some,

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:13.810
<b>Mustard</b>

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.730
but it's beyond the horizon.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.810
Then I'll use the toothpaste.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.520
Enough already!

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.640
Why do you have to be so lazy on the first episode of the year?!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.650
I understand the desire to be comfortable, but you're too comfortable!

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.870
You've been like this ever since we got the new kotatsu!

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.630
What if the little kids follow your example?!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.700
Can you pull it together?!

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.340
Where's the plug?

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:33.760
There isn't one.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.190
Don't lie to me!

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.250
Where is it?! Where did you hide it?!

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.260
I said that there isn't one.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.160
Don't play dumb!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.200
If there isn't a plug, how do you turn it on?!

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:50.020
There's no need to turn it off.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.520
Because

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:57.040
we're never leaving...

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:00.280
S-Space...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.000
No, this is...

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.290
This is a black hole!

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:26.260
That was "Your Brother is a ****"!

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:30.630
Thank you for listeningapoop!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.630
Thank you!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.980
Does everyone love me?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:40.570
We love you!

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:44.230
Does everyone love me?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.810
We love you!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:53.730
But the mothers in the PTA don't like this song very much.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.320
What are you doing, Pachi-boy?

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.290
Cut down the racket.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.510
Wait!

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.020
H-Hold on!

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.510
Wh-What is this?!

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:15.810
What's up with this kotatsu?!

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:19.150
How is there a black hole under the kotatsu?!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.090
What are you talking about?

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.650
That's how every kotatsu works.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.750
Once you get under one, you can never leave.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.710
A square black hole that sucks

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.390
motivation from humans and grants pure ecstasy.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:31.360
That's what a kotatsu is.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.910
I've never heard that scary explanation before!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.190
That's not what I mean!

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.550
There's something down there!

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.590
I'm literally stuck now!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.050
Where did you find this thing, Gin-san?!

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:51.930
<b>Anti-Evil Ward</b>

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.450
They needed to find a way to dispose of it, so they gave it to me for free.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.960
I really like the design.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:47.780
Isn't it nice?

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.750
The design?

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.930
There are a bunch of creepy wards everywhere!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.770
What was it she said?

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:59.070
The previous owner used this kotatsu to seal King Something-lo.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.900
It sounded scary, so I just ignored her and brought the kotatsu home.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.460
Uh, you heard the scary part!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.070
You only left out the "Picco"!

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:07.610
King Piccolo's in there!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.270
Don't worry, it's not King Piccolo.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.310
I think it was King Diablo.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:16.950
That's even scarier!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.040
And you're missing the point!

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.650
So what does this mean?!

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.100
Have we been sealed inside this kotatsu?!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.760
It's not that you don't want to get out, you can't!

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.520
What are we going to do?!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.730
We're supposed to spend

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:32.060
the first episode of the year sitting under a kotatsu?!

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.280
Not just the first episode.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.930
We'll be spending the entire year here.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:38.940
That can't last!

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:42.360
What's wrong with being lazy for a bit?

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:46.020
Pachi-boy, this is our sixth year.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.100
We may be following the Sazae-san tradition of never aging,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.320
but I'm almost 40 mentally.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:55.610
Mentally, I'm almost bald.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:59.020
Mentally?! You're physically bald!

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.890
I'm tired of working this combover every week.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.510
Can't I just not worry about my hair for once?

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:11.890
Yeah, after six years, I've learned how to talk straight.

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:15.380
I'm tired of sounding stupid.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.470
That's crazy talk!

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:21.510
I'm tired of living a lie!

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.520
Why are you bald?!

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.900
Wh-What are you people doing?!

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:29.050
You're supposed to be the main character and heroine in a Jump anime!

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:32.210
Shut up. Don't be such a nag.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.380
We took a whole year off so there

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.850
would be enough manga to resume the anime,

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:38.790
but now we're slacking again.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.080
When an episode in March

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.650
is based on a chapter from the first issue of Jump that year,

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.400
it's clear that there's a timing issue.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.610
We had two months to produce this episode?

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:48.330
Hey!

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.330
Stop it!

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.660
That's a really delicate issue right now!

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.640
You're not supposed to open that door right now!

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:56.050
They didn't plan ahead properly.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:58.020
Any kid could tell you that a

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.820
chapter won't give you an entire episode.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.400
The problem is when you have people

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:08.470
who don't plan ahead planning anime.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.400
Yeah, I'm getting sick of everything!

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:13.280
Th-This is bad.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:17.070
They're losing all their motivation to the evil kotatsu!

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:20.580
I need to get out of here before I go bald!

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.910
Forget the animation quality, this anime is in trouble.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.580
I need to call for help!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.460
Somebody's here!

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.290
Excuse me! Help us!

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.110
We can't move!

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.760
Please come in!

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:37.110
What's that? Is something wrong, Shinpachi-kun?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.190
Katsura-san!

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.360
This is pathetic!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.850
Gintoki, a warrior should not be living in squalor!

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:45.770
You should be ashamed!

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.360
Katsura-san, please listen to me!

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.980
Silence! You can make excuses later!

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.170
You've got it wrong!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.740
Listen to me first! Katsura-san, this is...

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:59.240
It's not Katsura. It's Zura.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.750
Brr, I'm freezing.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:04.460
He went bald instantly!

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.300
Hey! I told you to listen to me!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.750
Why are you immediately getting under the kotatsu?!

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.500
And what's with that gross forehead?!

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.780
Well, it's so cold outside.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.930
Too cold to be engaging in Joi activities.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:23.300
Though it's not just winter, since my body's starting to give out on me.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.140
My back hurts, my insurance doesn't cover anything,

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:28.250
and I got weird monsters pestering me.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.060
A trifecta of suck.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.530
Who is this old man?!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.530
Honestly, I envy you, Gintoki.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:38.160
I'm starting to think that I should have gotten a normal job.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.820
No, it's the same for everyone now,

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:42.200
given the economy.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.120
Hey!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.040
When did this turn into a reunion for old geezers?!

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:48.280
Sakamoto's the only one of us who's doing well.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.040
Takasugi went off his rocker.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.580
Though his family was always rich.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:00.010
So we work our entire lives and we're still worse off than those rich people.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.160
Pretty much.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:07.480
So we should go back to our kotatsu and rethink life.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:08.740
How do you go back to your kotatsu?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.270
Shouldn't you be going back to your hometown instead?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.940
But aren't you going to settle things with Takasugi?

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:16.410
Takasugi? Who are you talking about?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.070
I've forgotten who he is since he never shows up.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.610
I'll just write some bad stuff about him on an online forum

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.120
and that'll be the end of that.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.290
How does that settle anything?!

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.150
Yeah, if we bring him in, we'll have to

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:29.710
go through the trouble of a Joi past arc.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.380
Do you have anything in mind?

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.610
Hell no.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.750
What about you?

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:37.260
What actually happened in our past?

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:37.890
No kidding.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.050
Shut up! Just shut up!

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.010
You're not supposed to say that stuff!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:42.810
It's over!

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:45.080
This anime is falling apart!

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.560
Someone save us!

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:49.640
Oh, why are you making such a racket, Shin-chan?

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:50.720
Did something happen?

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.330
Sis! Kyubei-san!

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.970
Oh, everyone's together for a New Year's party!

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.450
What?! It's balding hell in here!

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:01.390
Sis, stay away!

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:03.780
If you get under the kotatsu, you'll never be able to leave!

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:04.920
It'll take away all your motivation

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.920
and turn you into a shell of a heroine!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.620
You should have told me sooner!

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.770
Huh? Who is that?

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.290
Where did that old man come from?

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.930
I'm sick of this.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.700
Why do I only get brief appearances?

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:20.720
What do you take me for?!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.050
Sis?!

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.640
You've already mastered that style?!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.150
You're more like an old man than a real old man!

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.520
And why won't any of you listen to me?!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.090
T-Tae-chan!

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.950
Kyubei-san! You're the only one who can help us!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.020
Please do something!

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:37.440
Man and woman. We can finally be together

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.700
How?! You're both old men now!

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.200
I screwed up!

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.110
Now, now.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.630
Forget about men and women and just relax.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.670
You're nothing more than an old man now!

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.840
But strangely enough, I feel satisfied

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:58.670
A kotatsu is a mysterious thing.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:01.750
If I can be under the same kotatsu as Tae-chan,

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:04.580
it doesn't matter if I'm a man or a woman.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.680
I just said that you're an old man!

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:11.840
I don't think I care about reviving the dojo anymore.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.560
The kotatsu has nothing to do with our dojo!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:19.180
Honestly, I'd given up around the third year of the anime.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:21.970
On the dojo and on my brother.

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:24.530
Why do you look so happy as you slander me?!

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:29.190
Yeah, it's not easy to be unmarried with a kid at that age.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.160
I'm not her kid!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.040
He said he would help you revive the dojo,

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:37.170
but he just stands around while his sister works at a cabaret club.

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.000
Could you stop badmouthing me?

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.050
I've heard that he spends his time fooling

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:44.530
around at some kind of odd job.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:46.520
He's like a cancer.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.970
Aren't you my boss?!

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:51.390
Why would you want to learn about samurai?

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.120
That's so general.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.180
It's like a person who says he wants to be a musician

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.820
and performs on the street instead of auditioning.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.370
What's wrong with performing on the street?!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.630
I'm gonna kill you!

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:06.660
You'd be better off just sitting under a kotatsu.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.450
That's right. Just kick back and relax.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:13.080
It's no use! The situation's only getting worse!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:15.570
Isn't there a savior out there to help?!

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:18.040
Shinpachi-kun, you don't need to worry.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.770
You aren't the only ones relaxing.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.010
You were down there?!

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.510
You two can't help! You need help!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:29.300
These are the characters who are always failing!

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:33.520
I'm getting tired of being a stalker.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:36.760
It's time for us to graduate.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.400
Did you forget that you just popped out from under the kotatsu?!

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:45.060
I've worked so hard to win his love.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.980
I did everything humanly possible.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.950
But I've finally noticed that there's

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:54.900
been someone else waiting for me.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:57.010
Nobody's waiting for you.

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:01.420
Once I realized that, I lost interest.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.490
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.970
Then the tables are turned.

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:09.230
We've always been on the pursuing side.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.550
It feels weird to be pursued.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.180
Nobody's after you!

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:17.180
And why are two bald people engaging in girl talk?

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:22.070
I see, so we're tired of pursuing and being pursued.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:26.590
Yes, I learned that lesson the hard way.

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:28.500
When I close my eyes, I can remember

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.510
the days spent in pursuit and being pursued.

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.210
Uh, Katsura-san, you've only ever been pursued!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.080
You've always got the cops on your tail!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:39.050
Then let's forget everything and relax.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:42.050
Why are you acting like you're not a criminal?!

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:54.350
That's right. We are no longer Shinsengumi and Joi.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.500
Starting today,

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.390
we're lazy bums.

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.130
That's not touching at all!

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.570
You're both just failing at life!

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.810
Oh, everyone's here.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:10.800
Hey, you're late, Hasegawa-san.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:12.320
Sorry, sorry.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.830
Why are you bald before you even got under the kotatsu?!

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:16.630
You didn't have any motivation to begin with!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.660
And what do you mean he's late?

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:19.720
Is there some way for lazy people to communicate with each other?!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.590
Okay, now that everyone's here, let's relax.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.330
What the hell is this?!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:34.260
Why do you have to act like this in the first episode of the new year?!

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.090
This is an anime.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.450
You're supposed to move.

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.510
I'll kill you.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:05.960
Oh, sorry.

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:10.720
Uh, you're breathing on me.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:16.730
Sadaharu-kun, could you move over a little?

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.370
Wait, there's no room over here.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:20.640
Oh, sorry.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:43.530
We can't relax.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.750
No shit!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:45.920
Leave!

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.750
You're taking up all the space so I can't even turn over!

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:52.550
I bought this kotatsu so I could relax!

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:55.550
Why are you people trying to relax in someone else's home?!

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.270
You always get to relax!

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.640
Why don't you leave?!

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.840
Excuse me! This is Gin-san's home!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.390
Outsiders should scram!

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:05.600
You're also an outsider!

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:08.160
How about we get rid of this dog first?!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.410
We should kick the gorilla out first!

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.580
Stop whining, freaks! None of you paid for this!

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.030
You didn't pay anything either!

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.730
I can't even get out of here!

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:17.710
What's wrong with this kotatsu?!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.580
Oh! Stop pushing!

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:25.830
Outta the way! I wanna relax!

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:52.020
Huh?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.660
What were we doing?

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.890
Hey, Shinpa—

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.590
I'm too lazy to say anything.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:09.920
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose</b>

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:07.310
Sorry.

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:44.930
<b>Next Time
Untitled</b>
